@ 30.1.2 - Pre-Proto-Bantu to Proto-Manenguba
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Hedinger, Robert (1987), The Manenguba Languages (Bantu A.15, Mbo Cluster) of Cameroon
	’p ’t ’d/d₂ c {’ɟ} ’k ɡ > f l ɟ s ∅ {w,∅} {k,w} / in C₁ position
	N:[+ lenis] > N:[- lenis] / in C₁ position
	p t ’t {’d,d₂} c k ’k > b d l {l,∅} ɟ ɡ ∅ / in C₂ position
	’m m ’n n {’ɲ,ɲ} ŋ > m {ᵐb,m} n {ⁿd,n} ɲ {ᵑɡ,ŋ} / in C₂ position
	{u,o} {ɛ,e,i} > w j / C_a in noun roots
	{u,o} {ɛ,e,i} > w j / C_(a) in verb roots
	{u,o} {ɛ,e,i} > w j / C_$V in noun class prefixes
	f > h (perhaps not in all languages?)